WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:19.987
The children had a delightful lunch with Mademoiselle.

2
00:00:19.988 --> 00:00:24.946
She served them cakes and tarts, and made wreaths for their heads.

3
00:00:24.947 --> 00:00:29.026
She drew pictures and told stories about her own school days.

4
00:00:29.027 --> 00:00:35.257
"Draw us a picture of a theater," said Gerald.

5
00:00:35.258 --> 00:00:38.314
"Do you like plays?" asked Mabel.

6
00:00:38.315 --> 00:00:40.993
"Oh yes, I love them!"

7
00:00:40.994 --> 00:00:44.183
Mademoiselle concentrated on her drawing.

8
00:00:44.184 --> 00:00:47.900
The children looked at each other and smiled.

9
00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:51.695
"We'll put on a play for you tonight," said Jimmy.

10
00:00:51.696 --> 00:00:56.743
"And please, may Eliza come too?" asked Kathleen.

11
00:00:56.744 --> 00:01:02.551
"Of course," said Mademoiselle with a smile.

12
00:01:02.552 --> 00:01:06.023
Mademoiselle stayed in the sitting room as usual.

13
00:01:06.024 --> 00:01:09.419
It was a good thing that she was not trying to concentrate!

14
00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:15.166
The children came in and out all afternoon, asking for things.

15
00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:19.344
May they have the sofa cushions?

16
00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.716
May they have the clothesline?

17
00:01:21.717 --> 00:01:25.074
Did she have any brightly colored scarves they could borrow?

18
00:01:25.075 --> 00:01:32.106
May they have tea in the garden because the stage was in the dining room?

19
00:01:32.107 --> 00:01:36.654
At last Eliza rang the dinner bell.

20
00:01:36.655 --> 00:01:41.604
That was the signal for Mademoiselle to go into the dining room for the play.

21
00:01:41.605 --> 00:01:45.319
Several tables had been pushed together to make a stage.

22
00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:50.570
Rows of chairs were set out for an audience.

23
00:01:50.571 --> 00:01:57.980
Mademoiselle was surprised to see seven people sitting in these chairs.

24
00:01:57.981 --> 00:02:02.342
"Children," she whispered through the stage curtains.

25
00:02:02.343 --> 00:02:06.066
"You should have asked me before you invited guests."

26
00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:08.093
The children laughed.

27
00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:13.761
"Turn up the lights," said Mabel.

28
00:02:13.762 --> 00:02:17.171
Mademoiselle looked again at the people in the audience.

29
00:02:17.172 --> 00:02:22.968
"Oh! They're not alive!" she cried in surprise.

30
00:02:22.969 --> 00:02:25.634
And indeed they were not.

31
00:02:25.635 --> 00:02:29.336
Their bodies were made of pillows and rolled-up blankets.

32
00:02:29.337 --> 00:02:32.220
Their spines were broom handles.

33
00:02:32.221 --> 00:02:36.721
Their arms and legs were hockey sticks and umbrellas.

34
00:02:36.722 --> 00:02:41.956
They were dressed in whatever coats, hats, and gloves the children could find.

35
00:02:41.957 --> 00:02:46.140
And their faces were paper masks made by Gerald.

36
00:02:46.141 --> 00:02:51.425
"You've made yourself an audience! Bravo!" said Mademoiselle.

37
00:02:51.426 --> 00:02:54.892
And she and Eliza clapped.

38
00:02:54.893 --> 00:02:57.694
They sat down and the curtain opened.

39
00:02:57.695 --> 00:03:03.673
"Beauty and the Beast," announced a voice from backstage.

40
00:03:03.674 --> 00:03:08.492
The children had spent much time making their costumes and audience.

41
00:03:08.493 --> 00:03:11.306
So they'd had little time to rehearse.

42
00:03:11.307 --> 00:03:14.832
But they had fun acting out the fairy tale.

43
00:03:14.833 --> 00:03:18.754
As Beauty, Mabel wore her princess clothes.

44
00:03:18.755 --> 00:03:22.600
As the Beast, Gerald wore some small rugs.

45
00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:26.199
Jimmy and Kathleen played all the minor parts.

46
00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:30.274
At the end of the second scene, everyone was backstage.

47
00:03:30.275 --> 00:03:34.339
"You should give me the ring," Mabel said to Gerald.

48
00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:37.048
He'd forgotten that it was in his pocket.

49
00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:41.955
"I'll do it in the next scene."

50
00:03:41.956 --> 00:03:46.102
And he did, making the ring part of the play.

51
00:03:46.103 --> 00:03:49.516
He told Beauty that the ring was a magic ring.

52
00:03:49.517 --> 00:03:52.210
It would give her anything she wished.

53
00:03:52.211 --> 00:03:57.862
So to see him again, she simply had to put it on and make her wish.

54
00:03:57.863 --> 00:04:01.237
At last they came to the final scene.

55
00:04:01.238 --> 00:04:05.895
Beauty was reunited with Beast, who was really a prince.

56
00:04:05.896 --> 00:04:09.434
Mademoiselle and Eliza clapped and cheered.

57
00:04:09.435 --> 00:04:12.687
Mabel looked at the fake audience members.

58
00:04:12.688 --> 00:04:15.333
"I wish those creatures we made were alive.

59
00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:18.230
We'd get some real applause then."

60
00:04:18.231 --> 00:04:21.632
"I'm glad they aren't alive," said Gerald.

61
00:04:21.633 --> 00:04:24.081
"I feel silly when I look at them."

62
00:04:24.082 --> 00:04:26.952
And suddenly it happened.

63
00:04:26.953 --> 00:04:29.642
There was the sound of more clapping.

64
00:04:29.643 --> 00:04:33.736
Seven paper faces were looking eagerly up at the stage.

65
00:04:33.737 --> 00:04:36.528
The creatures had come alive!

66
00:04:36.529 --> 00:04:43.054
Mademoiselle and Eliza screamed and ran from the room.

67
00:04:43.055 --> 00:04:46.518
"Give me the ring!" Gerald said to Mabel.

68
00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:49.195
He put the ring on his finger and cried,

69
00:04:49.196 --> 00:04:52.603
"I wish those Ugly-Wuglies weren't alive!"

70
00:04:52.604 --> 00:04:56.829
But nothing changed.

71
00:04:56.830 --> 00:05:02.222
Mabel and Gerald followed the creatures out into the hallway.

72
00:05:02.223 --> 00:05:12.846
"Excuse me," one said to Gerald, "can you recommend a good hotel?"
